diff --git a/rebuild/docs/ANALYTICS.md b/rebuild/docs/ANALYTICS.md
index 5cc17044..b9b26a08 100644
--- a/rebuild/docs/ANALYTICS.md
+++ b/rebuild/docs/ANALYTICS.md
@@ -1,7 +1,54 @@
-# Analytics ingestion and coverage
+# Analytics
 
-The single `/analytics` view sums the latest stored audience value once per selected channel and displays every stored Page metric and account-level advertising metric in the chosen range. Audience is a cross-channel sum, not deduplicated people. Publishing counts now use the same selected channels and range. Published items use `publishedAt`, scheduled items use `scheduledAt`, and failed items use `createdAt`.
+`/analytics` shows stored channel and advertising results for the channels, ad accounts and dates chosen in the sidebar. `/reports` redirects to it with the same selection, and the CSV export (`/api/reports/export`) is built from the same loader (`src/server/analytics/view.ts`), so the file always matches the screen.
 
-Facebook Page ingestion reads the Root-managed `meta.pageInsightMetrics` list. The default requests follows, media views, post engagements, and Page views; Root can change the list without editing code. Every dated value returned by Graph is stored under its own metric, provider period, and `end_time`. Numeric values and JSON breakdowns are retained. Repeating a sync updates the same observation rather than creating a new point under the sync date. Disabled Facebook engines do not run Page, Ads, or Inbox sync jobs.
+## What the page shows
 
-Provider support still requires live validation against this installation's approved scopes and API version. Page Insights requests are isolated per configured metric: a rejected metric no longer discards observations from successful metrics. A partial sync increments the job failure count, but a Root view naming the rejected metrics remains to be built. Root can remove unsupported entries from the metric list. Page sync follows Graph Insights pagination up to Root's configured page limit and rejects a response that exceeds that limit or points outside the configured Graph endpoint. Advertising sync is account-level; campaign, ad-set, and ad-level analytics remain incomplete. Other platform adapters and channel types do not yet contribute insights.
+- **Selected channel audience**: the latest stored follower count of each selected channel, added once per channel. People who follow several channels can be counted more than once; the page says so.
+- **Key numbers**: one card per measure with its plain name, value, change against the previous equal-length period (arrow, signed percentage and words, so colour is never the only signal), a small trend line and a one-line definition. Cards are toggles: up to three can be shown in the main chart. Measures the catalogue marks as headline measures come first; the rest sit behind "Show other measures".
+- **Trend**: a time-series chart of the chosen cards by day, an optional dashed previous-period line when one card is shown, and a table view of the same numbers. Cards with different units are drawn on separate scales (stated under the chart; values are in the tooltip and table). Running totals such as followers do not start the axis at zero.
+- **Compare channels / ad accounts**: one line, bar or table row per channel for any measure, with legend buttons to show or hide each one. Distinct-people measures keep each channel's own value.
+- **Top posts**: published posts for the selected channels and dates, sortable, with a link to the post. Interactions add up the comments (and likes where stored) held for each post. Per-post reach and views are not stored yet.
+- **Breakdowns** (for example followers by country), **No longer available** (retired measures that still have stored history, with the replacement named) and **Technical details** (stored names, period, source, latest day and last sync; the only place stored API names appear).
+- **Publishing records**: counts of published, scheduled and failed posts for the same selection.
+- **Ads**: ad-account selection stays in the sidebar; advertising measures appear beside channel measures, with money split by currency.
+
+Charts are plain SVG/React in `src/components/LineChart.tsx`, coloured only by the `--chart-1..6` theme tokens (kept at 3:1 against every surface by `tests/chart-tokens.test.ts`). Lines also differ by dash pattern and marker shape. Charts have a text summary, keyboard reading (arrow keys), a live readout, and a table alternative. Layout works at phone width: the chart is measured and redrawn at the container width, and tables scroll inside their own region.
+
+## Metric catalogue
+
+Platform modules supply their metrics through `PlatformModule.metrics` (`src/platforms/metrics.ts` defines the neutral shape; Facebook's entries, including its linked Instagram professional account and ad account measures, are in `src/platforms/facebook/metrics.ts`). Each entry has the stored name, a customer name, a one-line definition, a unit (`count`, `people`, `currency`, `rate`, `duration`), an aggregation rule, a group, and optionally a retirement (date and replacement), `headline`, `lowerIsBetter` (costs, lost followers) or `neutral` (spend) flags. A module may also provide `inferMetric` for stored names it does not list (ad actions are named from their action type). Shared code calls `findMetric(scope, key)` in `src/platforms/index.ts`; no shared UI names a platform. Names that nothing describes are shown in readable words and remain visible in Technical details.
+
+| Rule | Behaviour |
+| --- | --- |
+| `sum` | Events add across channels and days. |
+| `unique` | Distinct people are **not** additive. Totals are an upper bound shown as "up to N" (exact only for one channel and one day); every channel keeps its own value. |
+| `latest` | Running totals (followers): each channel contributes its newest value, channels are summed; the daily line carries each channel's last value forward. |
+| `rate` | Click-through rate, cost per click, cost per 1,000 impressions, cost per person reached and frequency are recomputed from summed parts, never averaged; a zero denominator gives no value. Rates that divide by distinct people are marked as estimates. |
+| money | Never mixed across currencies: each currency is its own measure ("Ad spend (EUR)"). Accounts that report no currency are shown without a symbol. |
+| rolling windows | Stored week or 28-day values are labelled with their window and use the newest value instead of being added. |
+| retired | Measures the platform has stopped serving appear as unavailable with an explanation and replacement, never as an empty chart. |
+
+Pure functions with unit tests: `src/server/analytics/overview.ts` (all rules above, previous period, change), `src/server/analytics/time.ts` (calendar-day arithmetic, previous period, zone-aware day boundaries including daylight saving and half-hour zones), `src/server/analytics/posts.ts` (ranking), `src/lib/analytics/format.ts` and `chart-math.ts`.
+
+## Dates and time zones
+
+A day is a calendar day in the workspace time zone. The range, the daily buckets and the previous period (same number of days, ending the day before the range starts) all use it. Channel values are placed on the day of their stored end time in that zone; advertising rows are already calendar dates and keep their own date. Ranges are capped at 400 days.
+
+## Export
+
+`/api/reports/export` returns a long-form CSV (`record_type, metric, channel, date, value, previous_value, change_percent, unit, currency, note, link`) with plain metric names: key-number summaries (with "up to" notes), each channel's value, audience, top posts, breakdowns, retired measures, daily values and per-channel daily values, in that order. When the Root row limit is reached the file ends with an explicit `truncated` row, dropping daily detail first. Provider text that looks like a spreadsheet formula is quoted.
+
+## Ingestion and coverage
+
+Facebook Page ingestion reads the Root-managed `meta.pageInsightMetrics` list. The default requests follows, media views, post engagements and Page views. Every dated value returned by Graph is stored under its own metric, provider period and `end_time`; numeric values and JSON breakdowns are kept, and repeating a sync updates the same observation. Disabled Facebook engines do not run Page, Ads or Inbox sync jobs.
+
+Provider support still needs live validation against this installation's approved scopes and API version. Page Insights requests are isolated per configured metric: a rejected metric does not discard successful ones. A partial sync increments the job failure count, but a Root view naming the rejected metrics remains to be built. Advertising sync is account level; campaign, ad-set and ad-level analytics are incomplete. Other platform adapters do not yet contribute insights.
+
+## Known gaps
+
+- Top posts rank by stored comments and likes only; post-level reach, views and reactions are not synced.
+- Ad measures stored as scalar fields without a catalogue entry (for example quality rankings) are not shown; action counts and action values are.
+- Demographic maps and pinned metrics from the legacy app are not rebuilt.
+- The MCP analytics tools still return the earlier metric list (`src/server/analytics/aggregate.ts`) and do not yet use the catalogue, comparison or previous-period rules.
+- Rolling-window and breakdown measures get no previous-period comparison beyond the totals the series shows.
