@@ -28,3 +28,7 @@ This interface uses a quiet editorial look for a focused social publishing works
 ## Composition guidance
 
 Use a single clear page title followed by supporting context and actions. Keep filters adjacent to the data they affect. Place important actions first in the action group and destructive actions last. Use table captions even when visually hidden, label every filter, and keep keyboard focus inside native modal dialogs. Use text or shape alongside status colors.
+
+## Charts
+
+`LineChart`, `ChartLegend` and `Sparkline` (`src/components/LineChart.tsx`) are plain SVG. Series colours come only from `--chart-1` to `--chart-6`, which every theme defines at 3:1 or better against its surfaces; each series also has its own dash pattern and marker shape, so meaning never rests on colour alone. A chart always has an accessible name and text summary, keyboard reading with the arrow keys, and a table alternative supplied by the page. Legend items are toggle buttons with `aria-pressed`.
